# @kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm — the kintsugi fracture body that
# resolves a malformed `restart_intensity` declaration to a proposed
# morphism that widens the period, raises the budget, or surfaces
# the malformation as a Tomm question per compiler-error-surface §8's
# three-mode algebra.
#
# THE OPERATIONAL HALF of bilateral pattern #53's FOURTH INSTANCE at
# supervision altitude. The declarative half lives at
# `@epistemologic/property/restart_intensity_well_formed` (sibling
# shard, same tick). This shard names the auto-fracture the
# kintsugi loop applies when the property's transparency surfaces a
# malformed-intensity opacity at supervisor declaration time.
#
# Closes the bilateral pair forward-promised by
# `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror` lines 269-272 (Seam audit
# `f732d9c` §Next-/loop).
#
# === The bilateral pattern (#53; fourth instance) ===
#
# First instance:  @kintsugi/fracture/keyword (2026-06-10 `d908798`;
#                  per-predicate).
# Second instance: @kintsugi/fracture/gate (2026-06-16; per-predicate;
#                  promotion tick).
# Third instance:  @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren (2026-06-19)
#                  + @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift +
#                  @kintsugi/fracture/operator_match (parametric-
#                  over-table variants).
# Fourth instance (THIS): @kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm at
#                  SUPERVISION altitude. The bilateral pair predicates
#                  over a typed CARRIER (not a source token or AST
#                  fragment) at runtime declaration; the fracture
#                  body's morphism proposes over the carrier's
#                  fields directly, without splinter(ast) rewriting
#                  source. This variant IS the pattern's supervision-
#                  altitude specialisation.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# Per the form/process partition (recognition #55 promoted at
# `20eaf15`): @kintsugi is the process-side family root. Fracture
# bodies emit morphisms the kintsugi loop applies — process-side by
# structure. Home: @kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm under the
# @kintsugi/fracture family root (per angle_to_paren / symbol_lift /
# operator_match / keyword / gate precedent).
#
# Naming discipline: `restart_storm` names the SUBJECT the fracture
# body prevents — the storm the paired property forbids by
# declaration-time well-formedness. Parallel to first-instance
# `keyword` (names the subject) and second-instance `gate` (names
# the subject); NOT the transformational shape of `angle_to_paren`
# or `symbol_lift` because there is no single canonical arrow
# (widen/raise/surface are three modes per compiler-error-surface
# §1's three-mode algebra; the fracture body dispatches over them).
# The subject-name is honest about the multi-mode discharge.
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Input: `opacity` (from `@glass`) — one located fact surfaced by
# `restart_intensity_well_formed(ri)`'s `failure(opacity_map)`
# verdict. Each opacity names ONE offending well-formedness
# conjunct: budget_positive, period_positive, or
# ratio_within_supervision_range. The `property` field carries the
# @nl description of which conjunct failed and (when the ratio
# conjunct fires) the observed vs ceiling ratio.
#
# Output: `morphism` (from `@kintsugi/consent`) — the typed candidate
# the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads from this body and proposes
# through `query_phi`. The morphism's content proposes one of three
# structural remedies per compiler-error-surface §8's three-mode
# algebra (per `9f4211d` amendment):
#
#   apply     — deterministic fracture-body application when the
#               remedy is unambiguous:
#                 - budget_positive violation ⇒ propose raising
#                   budget to the substrate's minimum-positive
#                   default (1) at the CARRIER;
#                 - period_positive violation ⇒ propose widening
#                   period to the substrate's minimum-positive
#                   default duration at the CARRIER;
#               Both are single-arrow rewrites of the malformed
#               carrier's field — deterministic; no observer
#               judgement required.
#
#   spawn     — escalate to a peer tournament when the remedy is
#               ambiguous: the ratio conjunct fires and the observed
#               ratio exceeds the ceiling. The substrate cannot
#               deterministically choose between "widen period" and
#               "lower budget"; both are legitimate remedies with
#               different operational trade-offs. The fracture body
#               emits a `spawn` morphism whose ground state IS the
#               malformed intensity + the ceiling; a supervision-
#               altitude peer tournament proposes candidate
#               (budget, period) pairs whose ratio satisfies the
#               ceiling; the tournament winner IS the substrate-
#               pull-correct discharge.
#
#   hold      — legitimate non-discharge when the malformation is
#               out-of-band-resolvable at substrate altitude —
#               specifically, when the ratio_ceiling itself is what
#               the supervisor should reconsider (the intensity is
#               "malformed" ONLY relative to this supervisor's
#               ceiling; a wider ceiling would let the declaration
#               stand). Per error-as-question.md §2 six-variant
#               answer algebra + compiler-error-surface §8: `hold`
#               emits `Partial(0.0, ref)` and the substrate carries
#               the crystal unresolved; the human observer at
#               reader-frame answers the Tomm-shaped question about
#               the ceiling's substrate-decl configuration.
#
# The mode-selection predicate lives in the fracture body's routing:
# `opacity.property` names which conjunct fired and (per the paired
# property's opacity_map contract) whether the mismatch is
# CARRIER-local (apply / spawn) or CONTEXT-local (hold — the
# ceiling belongs to the supervisor's substrate context, not the
# carrier).
#
# Spectrally: this fracture body IS one step along the Ricci flow at
# the supervision-declaration altitude. The substrate's curvature at
# a malformed-intensity site is the (budget-positivity ⊕
# period-positivity ⊕ ratio-boundedness) dissonance; the
# negative-curvature direction IS the three-mode discharge
# (apply/spawn/hold); the resolved site has zero curvature at this
# altitude (the intensity is well-formed OR the ceiling has been
# renegotiated at reader-frame).
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@glass`, `opacity` is the substrate's located-fact carrier;
# this shard reads it directly. Per `@kintsugi/consent`, `morphism`
# is the substrate's typed-candidate carrier; this shard emits it
# directly. Per `@kintsugi/morphism`, `morphism_context` is the
# per-candidate slice; the loop pairs this fracture's morphism with
# its pre-anchor at active_pass. Per the paired property
# `@epistemologic/property/restart_intensity_well_formed`, the
# consuming predicate's `well_formed(ri) -> verdict` is the gate
# that surfaces the opacity this body resolves.
#
# NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-`ref`
# carriers where structured types are available (per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] + [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]]).
# The fracture body reads typed opacity, emits typed morphism,
# discharges via the three-mode algebra — substrate vocabulary
# throughout.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly (DEFER adjudication) ===
#
# Reed's Phase B report DEFERRED: whether this composes cleanly
# with existing @kintsugi/fracture patterns (angle_to_paren,
# symbol_lift, operator_match) OR requires new pact-altitude
# primitive. Now that this shard exists at the signature altitude,
# the adjudication:
#
# **Composes cleanly with existing patterns; no new pact-altitude
# primitive required.**
#
# The signature `resolve_restart_storm(opacity: opacity) -> morphism`
# is byte-identical in shape to the third-instance fracture bodies
# (angle_to_paren, symbol_lift, operator_match). The bilateral
# vocabulary — opacity input, morphism output, opacity_map surfaced
# by the paired property's failure verdict — is exactly the same.
#
# What CHANGES at supervision altitude is the DISCHARGE MECHANISM,
# not the fracture-body contract:
#
# - Syntax-altitude fractures (angle_to_paren, symbol_lift,
#   operator_match) discharge via splinter(ast) — content-addressed
#   AST rewriting at @meta/ast altitude.
# - This supervision-altitude fracture discharges via three-mode
#   algebra (apply/spawn/hold) per compiler-error-surface §1 —
#   content-addressed proposals over a landed carrier's fields,
#   with mode selection based on the malformation class.
#
# Both discharge mechanisms sit AT THE MORPHISM'S CONTENT FIELD, not
# at the fracture-body signature. The morphism carrier absorbs both
# without vocabulary expansion — the compiler-error-surface §1
# three-mode algebra was ALREADY landed at `9f4211d`; this fracture
# body is the FIRST supervision-altitude consumer of the algebra
# via the bilateral pattern.
#
# The parametric-over-computation absorption (candidate note in
# #53's promoted architecture doc) covers this variant: the
# fracture body composes with the three-mode algebra at the morphism
# altitude, not at the signature altitude. Pattern #53's absorption
# holds; no new primitive.
#
# Adjacent gap surfaced honestly: the empirical composition of
# `spawn` mode with a live supervisor tournament is DEFERRED per
# [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]] — same DEFER
# emergent-supervision §5.5 H4 flags. The analytical shape composes;
# the operational witness lands when a runtime supervisor exercises
# the malformed-intensity discharge path.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   BEAM `init/1` rejection    Armstrong (1996) *Making reliable
#                              distributed systems* Ch. 4 §4.3.3.
#                              OTP's `supervisor` behaviour rejects
#                              malformed intensity at `init/1`
#                              return time with a startup error.
#                              This fracture body lifts the
#                              discipline: rather than one binary
#                              reject, the substrate proposes a
#                              structural remedy via three-mode
#                              algebra. Substrate-pull-correct
#                              addition: welcome, not just rejection.
#   Floyd-Hoare weakest-       Dijkstra (1975) *Guarded commands*.
#   precondition               The three-mode algebra IS the
#                              substrate's weakest-precondition
#                              discipline at supervision altitude:
#                              apply/spawn/hold are the three
#                              guarded-command branches over the
#                              opacity's classification.
#   circuit-breaker tuning     Nygard (2007) *Release It!* — the
#                              production-systems literature on
#                              circuit-breaker (max_restarts /
#                              max_seconds) sizing. The `spawn`
#                              mode's tournament IS the substrate's
#                              answer to the "correct sizing" question
#                              Nygard's book names as production-
#                              context-dependent.
#   Karl Tomm's therapeutic    Tomm (1988) *Interventive interviewing*
#   interviewing               — the reflexive-question modality this
#                              fracture body's `hold` mode invokes.
#                              Per compiler-error-surface §8: the
#                              observer's answer flows back as a
#                              substrate adjustment; the loop continues
#                              at reduced budget.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/kintsugi/compiler-error-surface.md §1 +
#               §8 (Mara `9f4211d` amendment; the three-mode algebra
#               `apply`/`spawn`/`hold` and its Tomm-question
