source @arxiv/beam/armstrong-thesis-1996
source @arxiv/programming/dijkstra-1975
source @arxiv/therapy/tomm-1988

glass @kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm {
  focus restart_storm
  project restart_storm
  split restart_storm
  shift restart_storm
  settle restart_storm
}

# === resolve_restart_storm — the fracture body ===
#
# THE AUTO-FRACTURE per bilateral pattern #53's fourth instance:
# given an opacity site at a malformed `restart_intensity`
# declaration (per the paired property's `failure(opacity_map)`
# verdict), emit the morphism that discharges the malformation
# via compiler-error-surface §1's three-mode algebra.
#
# Reads an opacity (one element of
# `restart_intensity_well_formed(ri).failure(opacity_map)`'s
# opacity_map); emits a candidate morphism the kintsugi loop
# proposes through `query_phi`. Mode dispatch on `opacity.property`:
#
#   - budget_positive violation OR period_positive violation
#         ⇒ `apply` — deterministic single-field rewrite.
#   - ratio_within_supervision_range violation, carrier-local
#         ⇒ `spawn` — peer tournament over (budget, period) pairs.
#   - ratio_within_supervision_range violation, context-local
#         (the ceiling belongs to the supervisor's context)
#         ⇒ `hold` — Tomm question surfaced to reader-frame.
#
# The morphism's `content` field carries the mode-specific proposal:
# for `apply`, a content-addressed rewritten carrier; for `spawn`,
# a peer-tournament ground-state reference; for `hold`, the
# `Partial(0.0, ref)` marker naming the unresolved crystal.
resolve_restart_storm(opacity: opacity) -> morphism { \ }

out @kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm
out resolve_restart_storm
